00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.405
Do they still give calendars at banks?

00:02:15.405 --> 00:02:16.238
I don't think so.

00:02:16.238 --> 00:02:17.640
Gourley, do they give calendars at banks?

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.945
I haven't been in a bank in 30 years.

00:02:19.945 --> 00:02:20.900
I don't know.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:25.420
You know when I first
came to Los Angeles with

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.180
Greg Daniels in 1985,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.590
and we went to Sunset Gower Studios

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.440
and we worked there as
comedy writers on a show

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.780
called Not Necessarily The News.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.100
They then gave us our
paycheck after a week

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.500
and Greg and I walked to the bank

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.620
and I remember going into the bank

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.030
and just thinking like, what is this?

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:45.240
Cause it was my first
job, my first real job,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.000
and walking in to open an
account and deposit it there.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:49.870
And then they told me, you know

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:50.960
you don't have to do this anymore.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:51.910
There's a machine out there.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:53.830
You put it in the envelope.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:54.663
Do you remember this?

00:02:54.663 --> 00:02:55.496
Yeah.

00:02:55.496 --> 00:02:56.553
Well, I don't remember.

00:02:56.553 --> 00:02:58.219
I wasn't there.
No, no, but you remember,

00:02:58.219 --> 00:02:59.534
I know you weren't there.

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:00.367
Oh.

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:01.200
I wasn't there either.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.033
Yeah.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:02.866
Well Gourley, you may have been there.

00:03:02.866 --> 00:03:03.910
You're kind of a weird guy.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.330
